    "Intermediate-risk patients with an unclear cause of syncope may benefit from a structured emergency department (ED) observation protocol to reduce hospital admissions. This includes short-term, expedited access to cardiac testing and consultations without adverse impacts on clinical outcomes. Important risk factors include age over 50, prior history of cardiac disease, presence of a cardiac device, family history of sudden cardiac death (SCD), and symptoms inconsistent with reflex-mediated syncope. Management strategies can involve structured ED observation or referral to specialists if no serious medical conditions are present.": "genes"
